From: LENA parallel agent <lena-parallel-agent@users.noreply.local>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:16:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] test(pg): real-PostgreSQL tests for lead and people
 services; fix attendance races

Adds disposable-cluster tests (skipped unless NILE_TEST_PG_ADMIN_URL is set),
same harness pattern as pool-resilience.pg.test.ts, kept out of engines/db.
- lead: forced and unforced concurrent moveLead -> exactly one winner, loser gets
  lead_stage_conflict; RLS isolation, WITH CHECK, fail-closed, no context bleed
  across pooled connections. Removing the WHERE stage=from guard is caught here
  (PGlite suite stays green with that mutant).
- people: forced races proved two defects in recordAttendance:
  * first record of an employee-day: loser failed with raw 23505
  * existing row: concurrent partial updates lost a field
  Fix: read the existing row FOR UPDATE; retry once on
  attendance_tenant_emp_day_uq. Both halves mutation-checked.
